{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_01a05df9e9a27240b59ffd3d","type":"tool_result","content":"title:\ttest(e2e): project-boundary dev probe counts dependency verification against its 60s HTTP budget\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\trickylabs\nlabels:\tarea:cli, area:tooling, gate:e2e, orchestrator:fixes, priority:p1, status:impl, type:test\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t0.0.7\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t1868\n--\n## Problem\n\nThe `behavior.project-boundary-dev` probe starts its 60 second deadline before launching the complete generated `dev` chain. That chain runs dependency closure and an O(files) node-modules verification before Vite starts. On NAS storage the retained #1865 fixture walked 638 packages and 42,053 files; the verifier exceeded the whole budget, while the child remained running and Vite never started. The probe then reported `Fresh dev server failed: fetch failed`, misclassifying slow preflight work as a server failure.\n\nThis is distinct from #1601: the fixture already has locked and materialized Vite 7.2.2, and no registry failure occurred. The probe and verifier are byte-identical on current main and #1865. Historic successful receipts complete this gate in 13.6 to 27.2 seconds, so runner and filesystem load determine the verdict.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Retained log: `/home/agent/observability/netscript-fixes/leased-proof-1865.log`\n- Retained fixture: `.llm/tmp/cli-e2e/plugin-smoke-20260901-083358` in the #1865 worktree\n- Current red: preflight reached `deps:verify`, emitted no completion or Vite banner, then timed out with child status still running.\n- Current main and #1865 have identical blobs for the probe, verifier generator, and workspace task generator.\n\n## Bounded repair\n\nKeep this separate from #1865. Replace the magic total-chain deadline with a named host-tolerant startup budget of at least the established 180 second tier, preserve immediate failure when the child exits, and report startup-chain timeout truthfully. Prefer separating dependency-preflight timing from Vite HTTP readiness if that remains bounded. Verifier optimization or memoization is broader follow-up work.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] Slow dependency verification does not consume the entire Fresh HTTP readiness budget.\n- [ ] A child process exit still fails promptly with its real exit status.\n- [ ] Timeout output distinguishes startup/preflight timeout from a Fresh server failure.\n- [ ] A focused regression reproduces the slow-preflight case without sleeping for the full production timeout.\n- [ ] The canonical scaffold runtime reaches Flow-B on the NAS and remains green on hosted CI.\n\nRelated to #1601 by defect family only; it is not the same root cause.\n=====PR=====\nGraphQL: Your token has not been granted the required scopes to execute this query. The 'login' field requires one of the following scopes: ['read:org'], but your token has only been granted the: ['repo'] scopes. Please modify your token's scopes at: https://github.com/settings/tokens., Your token has not been granted the required scopes to execute this query. The 'name' field requires one of the following scopes: ['read:org', 'read:discussion'], but your token has only been granted the: ['repo'] scopes. Please modify your token's scopes at: https://github.com/settings/tokens., Your token has not been granted the required scopes to execute this query. The 'slug' field requires one of the following scopes: ['read:org', 'read:discussion'], but your token has only been granted the: ['repo'] scopes. Please modify your token's scopes at: https://github.com/settings/tokens.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d76c1e2-cc74-4e83-bb1d-246737fa683c","uuid":"c98ace6f-b168-4786-95c5-446b0ced3c88","timestamp":"2026-09-01T17:17:36.104Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"title:\ttest(e2e): project-boundary dev probe counts dependency verification against its 60s HTTP budget\nstate:\tOPEN\nauthor:\trickylabs\nlabels:\tarea:cli, area:tooling, gate:e2e, orchestrator:fixes, priority:p1, status:impl, type:test\ncomments:\t0\nassignees:\t\nprojects:\t\nmilestone:\t0.0.7\nissue-type:\t\nparent:\t\nsub-issues:\t\nsub-issues-completed:\t\nblocked-by:\t\nblocking:\t\nnumber:\t1868\n--\n## Problem\n\nThe `behavior.project-boundary-dev` probe starts its 60 second deadline before launching the complete generated `dev` chain. That chain runs dependency closure and an O(files) node-modules verification before Vite starts. On NAS storage the retained #1865 fixture walked 638 packages and 42,053 files; the verifier exceeded the whole budget, while the child remained running and Vite never started. The probe then reported `Fresh dev server failed: fetch failed`, misclassifying slow preflight work as a server failure.\n\nThis is distinct from #1601: the fixture already has locked and materialized Vite 7.2.2, and no registry failure occurred. The probe and verifier are byte-identical on current main and #1865. Historic successful receipts complete this gate in 13.6 to 27.2 seconds, so runner and filesystem load determine the verdict.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Retained log: `/home/agent/observability/netscript-fixes/leased-proof-1865.log`\n- Retained fixture: `.llm/tmp/cli-e2e/plugin-smoke-20260901-083358` in the #1865 worktree\n- Current red: preflight reached `deps:verify`, emitted no completion or Vite banner, then timed out with child status still running.\n- Current main and #1865 have identical blobs for the probe, verifier generator, and workspace task generator.\n\n## Bounded repair\n\nKeep this separate from #1865. Replace the magic total-chain deadline with a named host-tolerant startup budget of at least the established 180 second tier, preserve immediate failure when the child exits, and report startup-chain timeout truthfully. Prefer separating dependency-preflight timing from Vite HTTP readiness if that remains bounded. Verifier optimization or memoization is broader follow-up work.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] Slow dependency verification does not consume the entire Fresh HTTP readiness budget.\n- [ ] A child process exit still fails promptly with its real exit status.\n- [ ] Timeout output distinguishes startup/preflight timeout from a Fresh server failure.\n- [ ] A focused regression reproduces the slow-preflight case without sleeping for the full production timeout.\n- [ ] The canonical scaffold runtime reaches Flow-B on the NAS and remains green on hosted CI.\n\nRelated to #1601 by defect family only; it is not the same root cause.\n=====PR=====\nGraphQL: Your token has not been granted the required scopes to execute this query. The 'login' field requires one of the following scopes: ['read:org'], but your token has only been granted the: ['repo'] scopes. Please modify your token's scopes at: https://github.com/settings/tokens., Your token has not been granted the required scopes to execute this query. The 'name' field requires one of the following scopes: ['read:org', 'read:discussion'], but your token has only been granted the: ['repo'] scopes. Please modify your token's scopes at: https://github.com/settings/tokens., Your token has not been granted the required scopes to execute this query. The 'slug' field requires one of the following scopes: ['read:org', 'read:discussion'], but your token has only been granted the: ['repo'] scopes. Please modify your token's scopes at: https://github.com/settings/tokens.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
